{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789834989,"nonce":"KS8rJ8hAqDE+2wzehrAQPOMXcwc=","message":"A fusion source the table above missed: OSR entries. The LLVM tier's OSR entry (and re-tier snapshot entry) compiles from the interpreter's shared Optimized AIR, which is built under AirConfigKey::standard() with fma=true regardless of ASH_AIR_FMA, and the LLVM emitter lowers Fma to llvm.fma. So on the NUC, hybrid --jit-tier llvm with ASH_AIR_FMA=0 plus the contract flag gated off (ASH_LLVM_CONTRACT=0, added for this measurement) still answered 112798564 for the full mandelbrot, deterministically; full-jit, hybrid-cranelift and AOT under the same switches answered 112790102. Making ASH_AIR_FMA=0 the default of AirConfigKey::standard() (air_pipeline::default_fma) brings the hybrid-llvm row to 112790102 too.\n\nConsequence: whichever policy is chosen, fusion has to be decided once in the shared AIR and every backend has to lower Fma identically. The LLVM tier lowering Fma to a hardware fma while Cranelift lowers it as mul+add is the same class of bug 8591530 fixed on the Cranelift side.","files":null}]}